Tested 14 projects, 4 contained vulnerable paths. the
# root policy does NOT cover the workspace sub-projects. nanoid is introduced in
# apps/web (via next > postcss), and the root file alone left both advisories
# active here."
# heading. This file is NOT in .github/sync.yml: the file-sync action
# overwrites whole files, and several repos carry legitimate per-repo policy
# (nswds-app's transitive postcss ignores, nswds-ui's Snyk Code exclude,
# engagement's and nswds-email's enumerated licence lists, dtl-sandbox's
# path-scoped entries). It is a Mechanism C file — see
# docs/config-single-source-of-truth.md.
#
# NOTE: do not add a '*:lic:*' catch-all. Snyk matches ignore keys as exact
# issue IDs and does not support globs — the catch-all that four repos carry
# is dead config (verified: nswds-app has it and `snyk test` still reports
# all 13 licence findings as active). Licence findings have to be enumerated,
# as nswds-email and engagement already do.

ignore:
  # ── nanoid CWE-835 — TWO DIFFERENT BUGS. Do not merge these reasons. ──
  #
  # Both advisories name nanoid@3.3.16, both say "upgrade to 5.1.16", and both
  # are titled "Infinite loop". They are not the same finding and do not have
  # the same answer. Verified against the published tarballs.
  #
  # Neither is fixed by an overrides entry pinning nanoid to ^5.1.16. nanoid
  # 5's exports map has no `require` condition — it is ESM-only, and postcss
  # (CJS, declares `nanoid: ^3.3.16`) consumes it via require(). That
  # resolution only works on Node >=22.12 and was never tested upstream.

  # -894 / CVE-2026-67214 — ALREADY PATCHED. `customAlphabet` and `nanoid` in
  # the `nanoid/non-secure` entry point hang on a negative size. Fixed in the
  # 3.x line by 3.3.16, which backports the same one-line change as 5.1.16:
  #
  #     -  while (i--) {
  #     +  while (i-- > 0) {
  #
  # 3.3.15..3.3.16 and 5.1.15..5.1.16 are the identical two-line patch in the
  # identical file. Snyk's `<5.1.16` range simply omits the backport.
  #
  # This entry is only correct where nanoid resolves to >=3.3.16. An older
  # 3.x is genuinely vulnerable and needs a lockfile refresh, not an ignore.
  # Check with `npm ls nanoid` before landing this block in a repo.
  SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506894:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          False positive against nanoid@3.3.16. CVE-2026-67214 is the negative-size
          infinite loop in nanoid/non-secure, backported to the 3.x line in 3.3.16
          (`while (i--)` -> `while (i-- > 0)`) — the same patch 5.1.16 carries.
          Snyk's `<5.1.16` range does not account for the backport.
        expires: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z

  # -897 / CVE-2026-67213 — NOT FIXED, NOT REACHABLE. A different function:
  # `customRandom` hangs on a size of 0. It is NOT patched in 3.3.16 —
  # `customRandom` is byte-identical between 3.3.15 and 3.3.16, and there is
  # no 3.x release that fixes it. The 5.x line was never affected: the
  # `if (!size) return ''` guard is present in 5.1.15 as well as 5.1.16, which
  # is why Snyk names 5.1.16 (the -894 fix) as the remediation for both.
  #
  # Accepted on reachability, not on version:
  #   * `customRandom` is exported only from nanoid's MAIN entry —
  #     `nanoid/non-secure` exports `{ nanoid, customAlphabet }` and nothing else.
  #   * postcss reaches nanoid only via `require('nanoid/non-secure')`
  #     (lib/input.js) and calls `nanoid(6)` with a hardcoded constant.
  # So the vulnerable function is not importable on the path that introduces
  # the finding. Re-check this if anything starts importing nanoid's main
  # entry — that changes the analysis, and the ignore stops being valid.
  SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506897:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Not reachable. CVE-2026-67213 is an infinite loop in `customRandom`, which
          is exported only from nanoid's main entry. The consumer that introduces
          nanoid here is postcss, which imports `nanoid/non-secure` — that entry
          point does not export `customRandom` — and calls `nanoid(6)` with a
          hardcoded constant, never attacker-controlled input. Not fixed in any
          3.x release; accepted on reachability.
        expires: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z

